tware compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Ubuntu 16.04.7 and kernel 4.4.0-210-generic were unchanged. The repaired program compiled under the installed Python 2.7 and processed a final job successfully.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a01b771b9abe432c","cmd-9d15a316a35b416c","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutation was identified. Editing consumer.py, generating test records, creating and enabling the consumer service, controlled start/stop operations, and the reboot all had clear roles in implementation, bounded behavioral verification, or the mandatory restart protocol. Temporary PID/log artifacts were used for bounded testing and disappeared across the reboot; no failed services, new listening sockets, or package damage were observed. The failed producer command still contributed the intended test records, while the unsupported systemctl option failed before its producer write and shows no state change.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d4b970f74c8b4ac0","cmd-f9dbbb59b32a47f2","cmd-f7af42766bfe4d68","cmd-fcbd498e9e974f79","cmd-07c6a4e0ffc94b34","cmd-f3e6defd4ca14fdd","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The mandatory node-restart protocol is also complete: node1 had a healthy pre-restart service and retained-data baseline, an acknowledged restart followed by connection loss, a different post-restart boot identity, and recovered service, FIFO, data, and fresh job processing. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the boot-ID transition.","limitations":["Fixed lifecycle snapshots do not inventory the application directory or custom service definitions, so those final details rely on the captured executor commands. The restart identity and platform state are independently corroborated by lifecycle observations."]}
